+## Local.4 candidate: connection and PCB inspection
+
+This local candidate separates idempotent **Connect** from explicit **Force Reconnect**. Activation remains inert; no auto-start is enabled. The legacy combined menu callback now behaves as Connect. Pending-action guards and explicit Stop remain in the transport.
+
+`pcb list --include-properties` reads the public native OtherProperty dictionary without changing it. An undefined getter result stays distinct from an empty dictionary; SDK errors and values outside the public JSON dictionary contract are rejected. This does not expose every private field or attest a transaction lock.
+
+`pcb export-netlist --project-uuid ... --pcb-uuid ...` requests original PCB netlist bytes through the official beta API. Project, PCB and active document/tab are checked before and after byte capture. No schematic/DSN substitute is returned; export alone does not establish electrical or manufacturing acceptance. Host availability and actual output format still require native verification.
+
+The earlier local.3 native RC result remains version-specific. Local.4 source and controlled tests do not replace native installation and readback.
+
+# Local qualification build 0.23.0-local.3
+
+This is a locally maintained test candidate, not an upstream release.
+
+Installation does not start a worker, scan ports, or connect to a daemon.
+After installation, use **EDA Agent → Connect / Reconnect** to request one
+connection attempt. **Stop** releases the socket, timers, Worker and Blob URL.
+A failed scan or lost heartbeat stops the connection; use Connect to try again.
+Auto-connect settings from the upstream build are deliberately not used here.
+The menu may evaluate the bundle again; one in-memory controller owns the
+connection and serves subsequent Stop/About actions in the same JS realm.
+
+The patch also prevents a completed context read or request from replying into
+a newer connection session. An accepted typed action can still execute later SDK steps after Stop. Stop
+does not cancel or roll back that action. Until it settles, About shows the
+pending action count and Connect refuses to start a new session. Keep the
+current document unchanged until it finishes. Context reads are single-flight
+within a session; a slow native read is not duplicated by every heartbeat.
+
+Local.3 also checks the observed project/document identity before a component
+modification. If the SDK throws, a bounded diagnostic performs at most one fresh
+component read and preserves the original SDK error. An unchanged, expected or
+partially changed observation does **not** turn the failed action into success.
+Unavailable identity, an incomplete snapshot or a diagnostic timeout stays
+unknown. These observations are not a transaction lock or cancellation, and the
+diagnostic does not retry, save or reload the document.
+
+The earlier local.1 import was reported to exit EasyEDA. These lifecycle defects
+have reproducible isolated tests, but the cause of that native exit is still
+unconfirmed. This build has **not** been installed or accepted in the native app.
+The user will perform installation. Original upstream documentation follows;
+its automatic startup/reconnection descriptions do not describe this candidate.
+
+---
+
